{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AC4 and AC6 re-measured at `origin/main` `0e7401446c5`\n\nBoth were previously reported here as \"blocked on an operator ruling\". That framing was\nwrong: it offered an AC amendment as a shortcut without first establishing whether the work\nwas buildable. Measured properly, the two ACs land in different places.\n\n### AC4 — substance is UNMET and buildable; only the \"Checked by\" clause has a real reason to change\n\nAC4 names five kinds. The rubric covers two:\n\n| AC4 kind | Covered by | State |\n|---|---|---|\n| refactor mechanics | `change-detector` | covered |\n| LOC floors | `loc-ceiling-pinning` (f86e) | covered |\n| re-export identity | — | **absent** |\n| import shape | — | **absent** |\n| re-run a gate script | — | **absent** |\n\nCase-insensitive counts over `code-review-tests.md`: `re-export` 0, `reexport` 0, `__all__`\n0, `import` 0, `gate script` 0, `re-run` 0, `rerun` 0. Not present under any synonym.\n\n**This is being built, not waived.** Story `e508-ce6c-2e52-4adc`\n(`biological-bleary-annelida`) is created under this epic, tagged `complexity-reduction`,\nto add the three missing entries plus their calibration cases.\n\nThe **\"Checked by\"** clause is the only part with a real reason to change. It names \"an\noverlay test asserting the taxonomy text is present in the criterion's rubric\". The rubric's\nown Rule-5 exception (`:97-103`) classifies exactly that test as a change-detector:\n\n> the grepped token is a real contract iff a NON-HUMAN consumer (a parser / validator /\n> downstream grep / registry / CI runner that branches on the exact value) reads it. An LLM\n> is NOT a non-human consumer — a prose/heading grep that merely guards the author's wording\n> IS a change-detector.\n\nMeasured: nothing but the LLM reads these headings. `git grep` over `src/ scripts/ tests/`\nfinds the rubric only in `criteria_routing.json`'s prose `_comment`, in `eval_specs/*.yaml`\nas fixture diffs, and in its own front matter. No parser branches on entry names. So the\nnamed check cannot be written without committing the antipattern it checks for.\n\nThe substitute is the project's own established route, recorded at `criteria_routing.json:112`\nfor both `3fce` and `f86e`: detection language in the rubric, calibration corpus in\n`eval_specs/code-review-tests.eval.yaml`. That demonstrates the taxonomy FIRES on real\ninstances and does not fire on lookalikes — a stronger claim than prose matching a string.\n\n### AC6 — genuinely obsolete, on evidence, not convenience\n\nAC6 requires the epic-close phase to merge held-out twin modules back into their parents.\nThe premise is that the held-out convention PRODUCES a twin. It no longer does.\n\n- `0b5d004f394 \"Retire the _heldout test-module naming convention\"` (ticket `d52f-823f`,\n  2026-11-02) renamed 5 modules to describe their subject and merged 1\n  (`test_code_review_provenance_heldout_2d1c.py`, which genuinely duplicated\n  `test_code_review_provenance.py` in scope). Only 1 of 6 was a duplicate; the other 5 were\n  merely badly named, so a blanket \"merge twins into parents\" step would have been WRONG for\n  5 of 6 cases.\n- `SKILL.md` 4c (`:258-262`) moves the **existing** edge/E2E tests out to\n  `$(git rev-parse --git-path heldout)/`; 4e (`:286`) **restores the full test set**. Same\n  modules out and back. No second module is created, so no twin exists to merge.\n\nChild `d278-3792-6538-4c8e` closed `obsolete` on this basis, with the measurement recorded\non its own ticket. I verified its load-bearing claim (4c/4e) directly rather than accepting\nit; it holds.\n\nAC6's deliverable was obsoleted mid-epic by a change that landed under a different ticket.\nThat is a real reason, and it is recorded here rather than absorbed into a close reason.\n\n### Position\n\n- AC4 substance → built by `e508-ce6c` (plan review starting).\n- AC4 \"Checked by\" → amend, citing Rule-5.\n- AC6 → withdraw, citing `0b5d004f394` and SKILL.md 4c/4e.\n- Epic closes after `e508-ce6c` lands, not before."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793748621973770844,"uuid":"cada64f7-a002-495f-b156-6d9b54332ef9"}